# tools/r/retired_rank_witness.rish -- does the counter rank two implementations the way the clock
# does?
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. This pier exposes no joule. tools/fixtures/e/energy_instrument_scan.sh reads
# joule_source=none, powercap_domains=0, msr_device=no, and tier=counters -- so every energy figure
# a lane writes here is a proxy, and the proxy this tree proposes is RETIRED INSTRUCTIONS. Row 3 of
# active-designing/20260917-105154_the-refusal-that-can-fire.md makes that proposal and states its
# own falsifier in one sentence: the counter ranks two implementations in the opposite order from
# wall time. This rung is the reading that fires it.
#
# WHAT WAS ALREADY STANDING, AND WHAT WAS MISSING. tools/rye/perf_self_count.rye and
# tools/rye/retired_count.rye open a counter scoped to THIS process and count a loop compiled into
# it. They proved the counter tier is reachable and measured the two spreads. Neither can measure a
# COMMAND, and ranking two implementations is exactly that. tools/rye/retired_exec.rye forks, arms a
# counter on the dependent with enable_on_exec and inherit, releases it through a pipe to exec, and
# reports instructions beside wall nanoseconds for that dependent and everything it starts.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal. Nineteen behaviors over planted arm pairs whose right answer is arranged
# before the run: five refusals bitten, the agreeing case named from both positions so a scan that
# always names its first arm reds, the DISAGREEING case shown firing on a sleeper-against-worker
# pair, two arms that are one arm declining to be ranked, and one mutation -- an order function that
# always names the first arm -- shown to bite.
#
# WHY THE DISAGREEMENT LEG IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. A reading that could never say `agree=no` says
# nothing when it says `agree=yes`. The sleeper pair is the proxy's true boundary, named in the
# scan's own header: user-space retired instructions exclude kernel and hypervisor, so a workload
# that waits rather than computes reports a small count beside a large clock. That is a property of
# the unit rather than a defect, and the instrument states it out loud.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That retired instructions track joules -- no joule is readable here, so that
# stays a stated assumption of the row rather than a measurement, and the row's confidence says so.
# Nor that a counter read on a shared virtual host could be attributed to one tenant.
#
# A HOST IS NOT A FAULT (REDS %646). Where the kernel refuses the counter the scan reports
# tier=cpu_seconds and verdict=counter_unavailable rather than inventing an order, and this witness
# reads the control's own legs rather than the pier's luck.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/retired_rank_witness.rish

say "retired-rank: Language EN -- a unit that ranks two implementations backwards is the wrong unit."
say "retired-rank: Style Gauge, Meter -- the reading names its tier and its separation before any order is claimed."
say "retired-rank: Lens TAME -- safety first: an order manufactured out of noise is worse than no order."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/retired_rank_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "retired-rank: the control must run -- see its own lines"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "retired-rank: every planted arm pair must read the way it was built to read"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "retired-rank: a leg that failed is a behavior nobody proved"
assert control.out contains "leg=disagree_word reading=agree=no ok" else "retired-rank: a reading that cannot say no says nothing when it says yes"
assert control.out contains "leg=order_not_position" else "retired-rank: the cheaper arm is found by its number, never by its position"
assert control.out contains "leg=mutation_bites" else "retired-rank: a mutation that passes is a leg that was never load-bearing"
assert control.out contains "leg=too_close_verdict" else "retired-rank: two arms that are one arm earn no order"

say "retired-rank: GREEN -- the ranking reading refuses, agrees, and disagrees, each proven by doing."
